@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@                                                                                               
 # Living Survey: Quantum_Computing                                                                            
                                                                                                               
 ## Introduction                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
 This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Quantum_Computing**.                             
+                                                                                                              
+## Quantum Algorithms & Toolchains                                                                            
+Recent studies have focused on the practical adoption and developer ecosystems surrounding quantum            
technologies. An empirical investigation into Stack Overflow repositories highlights that hybrid               
quantum-classical computing and circuit implementation are the most prevalent topics, with Qiskit and Q-sharp  
dominating discussions [[^https:__openalex.org_W7155247427]]. Furthermore, tracking trends across open software
platforms and financial news provides pivotal insights into the emerging quantum landscape                     
[[^10.1007_978-3-031-90727-2_20]].                                                                             
+                                                                                                              
+## Quantum Simulation & Optimization                                                                          
+Significant progress has been made in applying quantum paradigms to complex simulations and optimization      
problems. The PULSEE software package facilitates the simulation of magnetic resonance observables, bridging   
quantum information science with condensed matter research [[^10.1016_j.cpc.2022.108598]]. In optimization,    
granular computing schemes have been shown to statistically enhance quantum evolutionary algorithms for        
continuous functions [[^10.1007_s41066-022-00348-9]]. Additionally, quantum annealing has been practically     
applied to the configurational analysis of defective graphene structures, offering a guide for computational   
chemists [[^10.1063_5.0151346]].                                                                               
+                                                                                                              
+## Quantum Cryptography & Internet                                                                            
+The development of secure quantum communication networks remains a critical frontier. Research outlines the   
theoretical foundations and practical steps toward a global Quantum Internet, promising ultra-secure           
connectivity for quantum devices [[^10.31695_ijerat.2025.9.1]]. Comprehensive analyses of quantum cryptography 
protocols, including BB84, B92, and B91, alongside Shor's algorithm implementations on quantum hardware,       
continue to refine security standards [[^https:__openalex.org_W7112574406]]. Practical simulations of the BB84 
protocol, modeling eavesdropping and channel noise, further demonstrate the viability of provably secure       
communication [[^10.6084_m9.figshare.32051724]].                                                               
+                                                                                                              
+## Applications in Engineering & Materials                                                                    
+Quantum computing is increasingly explored for specialized engineering challenges. In computational fluid     
dynamics (CFD), quantum algorithms based on the Lattice Boltzmann Method and Navier-Stokes equations are being 
developed to simulate complex thermal fluid systems, such as aeronautical heat exchangers                      
[[^10.11159_icffts23.133]][^10.21741_9781644902813-38]]. Beyond traditional computing architectures, novel     
paradigms like atom computing propose replacing transistors with controlled electron flows to overcome material
scaling limits [[^10.34257_gjsfra257362]]. Comparative studies also continue to evaluate the architectural     
distinctions between digital, quantum, and biological computing systems [[^10.1109_mc.2021.3083430]].          
+                                                                                                              
+## Post-Quantum Cryptography & Security                                                                       
+As quantum capabilities advance, the security of classical cryptographic standards is under scrutiny. The     
CypherGliph system introduces hybrid iterative cipher chaining combined with post-quantum cryptographic        
strategies to mitigate threats from Grover’s and Shor’s algorithms [[^10.56975_tijer.v13i3.161368]].           
Concurrently, improved dual lattice attacks on Learning With Errors (LWE) problems have demonstrated reduced   
security margins for leading post-quantum finalists like Kyber and Dilithium, emphasizing the need for rigorous
cryptanalysis [[^10.5281_zenodo.6493704]]. A comprehensive review of quantum computing applications also       
underscores the transformative potential and future disruptions across various scientific and industrial       
domains [[^10.5120_ijca2021921834]].                                                                           
                                                                                                               

