+  author={Unknown},                                                                                           
+  journal={IJERAT},                                                                                           
+  year={2025},                                                                                                
+  abstract={Today’s Internet is a global communications network used to transfer, process, and store classical
information. The quantum Internet is a hypothetical high-speed Internet that provides ultra-secure connectivity
to quantum devices across the globe. It is a network of quantum computers that will someday send, compute, and 
receive information encoded in quantum states. It is a communications network that will transform industries,  
increase security, and alter the way we transmit information. While quantum computers exist in the physical    
world, the concept of quantum Internet is currently theoretical. In its infant form, the quantum Internet      
promises to make the digital domain safer, more productive, and more powerful than ever before. In this study, 
we provide a primer on quantum Internet, which provides a large-scale application of advanced quantum          
communication technologies and protocols.}                                                                     
